      {
        "name": "item?",
        "type": "| Omit< PartProps<\"li\", CoreBreadcrumbItemProps>, \"id\" | \"ref\" | \"aria-labelledby\" | \"aria-describedby\" >",
        "notes": "Applied to EVERY level, hence no `collapsed` — the entry's own field, already excluded through `Own` — and no `id` **or IDREF**: one id repeated down a list is a broken reference per level, and one `aria-labelledby` repeated gives every level the same name, which no dangling-IDREF check can see because the id it points at does resolve. `ref` goes because a single ref held by N items ends up holding the last one.",
        "source": "composed.tsx:78"
      },
      {
        "name": "link?",
        "type": "| Omit< PartProps<\"a\", CoreBreadcrumbLinkProps>, \"id\" | \"ref\" | \"href\" | \"current\" | \"aria-labelledby\" | \"aria-describedby\" >",
        "notes": "Applied to EVERY link, and excluded for the same reasons — plus `href` and `current`, which are the two the layer derives. A fixed `href` here would point every level at one place, and a fixed `current` would publish a trail with as many current levels as it has entries.",
        "source": "composed.tsx:90"
      }
    ]
